          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "When it is hot, a dog cannot sweat to cool down but uses moisture evaporation from its tongue to regulate its body temperature. This is not effective for large animals.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-q14-enlargement",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Consider what would happen if a dog’s dimensions were increased by a factor of 10.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "By what factor would its volume be increased?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1000$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Volume scale factor}&=10^3\\\\&=1000\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "By what factor would the surface area of its tongue be increased?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$100$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Surface-area scale factor}&=10^2\\\\&=100\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What effect would this have on the animal?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The dog would overheat: its volume increases faster than the surface area available to dissipate heat.",
          "worked": "Its volume increases by a factor of $1000$, but its tongue’s surface area increases by only $100$. The tongue therefore has one-tenth as much surface area per unit volume. The dog would produce far more heat but have relatively less surface area to dissipate it, so it would overheat.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
    ]
  },
